# THE STORE OF THE PAIR'S SOURCE APART FROM ITS INTERPOLATION: TWO GENERATED FRAMES OF ONE PAIR, AND A PAIR WITH NONE (2026-10-18, frame
# generation phase 5, the true fill's package G1: docs\reports\fg-5\brief-truefill\PLAN-truefill.md, B.1 and C).
#
# WHAT AMD'S CODE DOES. One dispatch makes one generated frame and, as its LAST JOB, keeps the pair's picture (the HUD-less
# one where it is bound, else the presented one) as "the previous interpolation source", which the NEXT pair's
# dispatch interpolates from (ffx_frameinterpolation.cpp at v2.3.0, 1273 to 1285; since the exact cut
# fi-inpainting-keeps-the-source, with a HUD-less image of 16-bit floats the inpainting pass stores it pixel by pixel
# instead, and the copy is not scheduled). A second dispatch of the same pair would then interpolate from the pair's
# own picture to itself. The same dispatch keeps one more thing for the pairs after it: THE COUNT OF DISPATCHES SINCE
# THE LAST RESET (COUNTER_FRAME_INDEX_SINCE_LAST_RESET, by the setup pass's thread of pixel (0, 0): 0 on a reset or a
# scene change, else one more). The interpolation reads it (0: the current picture is copied; under 10: optical flow's
# colour is left out), and so does the product's v-env (its frames after a reset). A second dispatch of one pair would
# count the pair twice.
# WHAT ELSE A DISPATCH LEAVES FOR THE NEXT PAIR, READ FOR THIS CUT (each is right after every form below):
#   - AMD's previousFrameID and dispatchCount (the reset rule, 1008 to 1013): a second dispatch of one id has
#     frameID - previousFrameID = 0, so it is neither "decreased" nor "skipped" and DOES NOT RESET; dispatchCount is
#     only tested against 0. The glue's ResetsNow (dlssiv_fg.cpp) is AMD's rule with the glue's own lastId, written by
#     every interpolate call, so the same holds there. A dispatch that only keeps the history goes through the same
#     head and writes both.
#   - COUNTER_SPD, the inpainting pyramids' atomic count: the setup pass writes 0 and each pyramid's last group puts it
#     back to 0 (ffx_spd.h, SpdResetAtomicCounter), so it is 0 between any two dispatches whatever runs.
#   - The eight "aliasable" images and the reconstructed depth of the generated frame: every dispatch discards and
#     clears or writes them whole before it reads them (fi-setup-by-clears' five clears, AMD's own clear of the depth).
#   - The prepare's three images (two sets, switched by the prepare) and optical flow's own history: written by the
#     prepare and the optical flow call, once a pair in every form below; the interpolate reads them only.
#   - v-env's envelopes (the product): written by the optical flow call alone.
#   - the debug bar's colour (a static of AMD's file): it steps at every dispatch; it shows only with a debug drawing.
#   - the constant buffer and the descriptors: from AMD's rings, 1.6 MB and 204,800 descriptors for the two effects,
#     which a pair of three calls uses some 1 percent of; a fourth call a pair leaves them dozens of pairs deep.
#
# THE CUT. AMD's dispatch description gains storeApart (at the end of the struct; 0, the struct's zero, is AMD's dispatch
# exactly), three bits:
#   NO_STORE    the pair's source is NOT kept: no copy at the end, and with a HUD-less image of 16-bit floats bit 29 of
#               the dispatch flags tells the inpainting pass not to store it (the pass's own path is kept whole, so the
#               product's fi-cover-in-alpha, which lives in that path, covers the first of two generated frames too);
#   STORE_ONLY  no generated frame: of the passes, the setup (one group, for the count) alone, and then the copy of the
#               source (the inpainting pass that would store it does not run). No discard, no clear, no other pass: what
#               they would write is discarded and written again by the next dispatch before anything reads it;
#   AGAIN       a later dispatch of a pair whose first dispatch kept the count: the setup pass is not dispatched (its
#               zeroes are the five clears' since fi-setup-by-clears, so nothing else of the dispatch changes), and the
#               interpolation reads the count the pair's first dispatch wrote.
# OUR GLUE (define DLSSIV_FG_CUT_STORE_APART; ffx-own\glue\dlssiv_fg.h, INTERFACE 3) asks for them by the flags
# DLSSIV_FG_NO_STORE and DLSSIV_FG_STORE_ONLY of an interpolate call, and sets AGAIN itself for the next interpolate of
# the id a NO_STORE call left open. A pair left open and never closed (another id comes) resets that id's dispatches: the
# source kept for it is not its previous frame's.
# THE THREE FORMS. A pair with ONE generated frame: as before (no flag). TWO: interpolate(1/3, NO_STORE), interpolate(2/3);
# each equals a single interpolate at its t, pixel for pixel. NONE (the flow-only pair): prepare, optical flow,
# interpolate(STORE_ONLY): the next pair's picture equals the one it has after a full dispatch, pixel for pixel.
# IT DEPENDS ON fi-setup-by-clears AND fi-inpainting-keeps-the-source: its old texts are theirs, so a set without them
# refuses it (cuts.py: "its old text is in ... 0 time(s)").
# WHAT IT COSTS: nothing at the defaults (a test of a constant word in the C++, one uniform branch around a store in
# the inpainting pass's 16-bit HUD-less path). The forms' prices are the stamps of tools\test-fg-own\fgtime.cpp --form.
# THE JUDGE: with no flag the exact library must equal the reference in every pair and the product's pictures must be the
# pinned ones (tools\test-fg-own\run.py --ours); the forms are held by tools\test-fg-own\thirds.py, whose control (a first
# interpolate that stores) must fail the second.
what the store of the pair's source for the next pair is apart from its interpolation: a dispatch may keep it (AMD's), not keep it (the first of two generated frames of one pair), or only keep it with the pair's count (a pair with no generated frame); a later dispatch of the pair does not count it again
passes ffx_frameinterpolation_inpainting_pass
wave64 it edits the inpainting pass's file, which both the cs_6_2 and the cs_6_6 (wave64) variants are compiled from, and AMD's C++ that runs on every device; no wave operation; not run here on a wave64 device
define DLSSIV_FG_CUT_STORE_APART
file framegeneration/fsr3/include/ffx_frameinterpolation.h
--- old
    float                               interpolationPosition;              ///< (the mod's cut fi-position) where the generated frame stands: 0 the previous frame, 1 the current; 0, or anything not inside (0, 1), is AMD's middle (0.5)
} FfxFrameInterpolationDispatchDescription;
--- new
    float                               interpolationPosition;              ///< (the mod's cut fi-position) where the generated frame stands: 0 the previous frame, 1 the current; 0, or anything not inside (0, 1), is AMD's middle (0.5)

    uint32_t                            storeApart;                         ///< (the mod's cut fi-store-apart) 0: AMD's dispatch. FFX_FRAMEINTERPOLATION_STORE_APART_ bits: NO_STORE, STORE_ONLY, AGAIN
} FfxFrameInterpolationDispatchDescription;

// (the mod's cut fi-store-apart) the bits of FfxFrameInterpolationDispatchDescription::storeApart
#define FFX_FRAMEINTERPOLATION_STORE_APART_NO_STORE     1u      ///< the pair's source is not kept for the next pair (the first of two generated frames of one pair)
#define FFX_FRAMEINTERPOLATION_STORE_APART_STORE_ONLY   2u      ///< no generated frame: the pair's count and the store of its source alone (NO_STORE is then not read)
#define FFX_FRAMEINTERPOLATION_STORE_APART_AGAIN        4u      ///< a later dispatch of a pair whose first dispatch counted it: the count is not kept again
--- end
file framegeneration/fsr3/internal/ffx_frameinterpolation.cpp
--- old
    if (inpaintingKeepsSource)
    {
        contextPrivate->constants.dispatchFlags |= 0x40000000u;
    }
--- new
    if (inpaintingKeepsSource)
    {
        contextPrivate->constants.dispatchFlags |= 0x40000000u;
    }
    // (the mod's cut fi-store-apart) what of the pair this dispatch keeps for the next one. STORE_ONLY: the count and the copy of
    // the source, no generated frame. NO_STORE: no copy, and the inpainting pass told by bit 29 not to store (its path is
    // otherwise the one bit 30 asks for). AGAIN: the setup pass, which keeps the count, is not dispatched.
    const bool storeOnly    = (params->storeApart & FFX_FRAMEINTERPOLATION_STORE_APART_STORE_ONLY) != 0;
    const bool storeSkipped = !storeOnly && (params->storeApart & FFX_FRAMEINTERPOLATION_STORE_APART_NO_STORE) != 0;
    const bool countKept    = (params->storeApart & FFX_FRAMEINTERPOLATION_STORE_APART_AGAIN) != 0;
    if (inpaintingKeepsSource && storeSkipped)
    {
        contextPrivate->constants.dispatchFlags |= 0x20000000u;
    }
--- end
